Every step swaps two ~adjacent~ positions \-\- the defining property that makes SJT
a Gray code for permutations, stronger than Heap's "any single swap". The value 4,
being largest, is mobile most often and sweeps the full width of the array
repeatedly, the permutation odometer's fastest wheel.


Each coloured line is one value's position across the 24 permutations. Every line
moves by at most one row per step \-\- the visual fingerprint of adjacent-only
transpositions \-\- and the largest value (gold) traces the widest zig-zag, gliding
from one end to the other and back as the smaller values tick over beneath it.
